head
  title About
  meta(name="description" content="Kévyn, a French full-stack developer: how I got into coding, and what I care about in it.")
article.mx-auto.max-w-2xl
  h1.mb-10.text-3xl.font-semibold About
  .prose
    p I'm Kévyn, a French full-stack developer based in Bordeaux.
    h2 How I got here
    p It started with an Arduino at a family meal. I spent the following year tinkering with it, then moved on to really basic HTML, Discord bots hosted on Glitch, and a lot of Processing.
    p In my first year of high school (seconde), one class had us use Processing. I made a platform game for it, and the teacher didn't believe I had written it myself. The code was the worst, it would burn my eyes today. Around then, a YouTuber bought a VPS for me to set up the Discord bot I had made for them.
    p Early on, a friend also bought me a VPS of my own, and it helped me a lot once I got to university, a computer science IUT, where I was bored enough to play Dofus during classes. Then came a one-year work-study web degree (licence pro en alternance), and straight after it the job I still hold, four years in now.
    h2 What I care about
    p Developer experience, performance and accessibility. And the environment: making things small and keeping their footprint down.
    p I'm strict about code in general, and about its formatting most of all: code has to breathe. That's why I made #[a(href="https://github.com/Kayno0o/eslint") my own ESLint ruleset], first as a layer over antfu's, then rewritten from scratch. At work, I set up a really strong PHP CS Fixer config, to annoy my coworkers, or rather so I don't grumble at them when I read their code.
